From 8fe6fcb41e13fa478e2b6468e47d4ef42c48b22f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A creature's swing trails its last stroke, and a beast trails
 what strikes

A creature's PlayUnitAnimation trail now starts trailMs before the impact and fades just
after it, instead of starting with the wind-up (a coiled wind-up's hold drew a smear, and a
long one was over before the blow). A creature holding a weapon trails it, as a hero does;
one holding none (a boar, a wolf, a bear) trails the part of it that strikes: the bone whose
pivot moves farthest against the body over the clip's last stroke, along the link from its
parent. A blow called off before its stroke draws nothing. HasActionCombat() is 9.
